---
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const pageTitle = "Privacy and RFQ Delivery Status | XINGXU FAN";
const pageDescription =
  "Understand what the XINGXU FAN RFQ workflow validates, sends and deliberately does not store before public launch.";
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <main>
    <article class="policy-page">
      <header>
        <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Privacy" }]} />
        <h1>How the RFQ Workflow Handles Inquiry Information</h1>
        <p class="policy-page__lede">
          The checked-in default remains local-only. Production submission is enabled only after the prepared live
          Turnstile and email configuration is deployed on the authorized domain and its delivery and privacy process
          are accepted end to end.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>Current local-development behavior</h2>
        <p>
          The quote page submits to a same-origin Worker endpoint. The server bounds and validates the request, checks
          the Turnstile response and then attempts email delivery only when the delivery mode is valid. The checked-in
          configuration uses local-only hostnames and Wrangler's simulated email binding, so a complete local test can
          reach the confirmation page without sending the inquiry outside the development computer.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Information requested</h2>
        <p>
          The form asks for buyer and company context, country or region, email or WhatsApp, product direction,
          quantity, destination, requirement summary and an acknowledgement of this notice. Selection-help requests
          may add application, airflow, pressure, electrical, dimensional, material and operating-medium details.
          Do not enter confidential or export-controlled information beyond what is necessary for a quotation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Processing and storage boundary</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The server verifies required fields and Turnstile before an email delivery attempt.</li>
          <li>The application does not add an inquiry database, file upload or attachment storage.</li>
          <li>Operational logs contain request status and a reference ID, not full contact details or message text.</li>
          <li>A successful screen is shown only after the configured email service accepts the message.</li>
          <li>Email retention and access follow the destination mailbox policy; that policy and its access owner must be approved before public launch.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Requirements before public submission</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Approve the business identity responsible for the inquiry and an accessible privacy contact.</li>
          <li>Deploy the prepared production configuration and connect the authorized domain to the intended Worker.</li>
          <li>Use the prepared production Turnstile widget sitekey and Worker secret only in their approved build and runtime locations.</li>
          <li>Activate the approved sender and verified Gmail destination through the restricted email binding.</li>
          <li>Run a real-delivery test and approve this notice, retention wording and rights-request process.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact and rights requests</h2>
        <p>
          No public privacy contact has been approved for this build. A working contact route and response owner must
          be published before the inquiry form is activated. Until then, this page records an implementation boundary
          rather than a complete production privacy notice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <footer class="policy-page__footer">
        <p>Last reviewed for the local Stage 4 build: 14 September 2026.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Review contact status</a>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
